{"ids":["one-neuron","feature-normalization","dot-product","matmul","softmax","cnn","sigmoid"],"purposes":["One neuron: a linear fit ŷ = wx + b trained by gradient descent on the squared error.","Feature normalization: each of three features is centred by its mean and scaled by its spread, every position on its own.","Dot product: a weighted sum s = ∑ wᵢxᵢ, one multiply per pair and one running sum.","Matrix multiply: every cell of C is a dot product, the row of A with the column of B, summed over k.","Softmax: turn a vector of scores into probabilities, each score exponentiated and divided by the sum of all of them.","Convolution: every output cell is a weighted sum over a small window of the input, the same kernel slid over every position.","Sigmoid neuron: ŷ = σ(wx + b), a logistic fit trained by gradient descent on the squared error, through the squashing function."],"schema":"sw-ml-study.rosetta.stones","titles":["One neuron","Feature normalization","Dot product","Matrix multiply","Softmax","CNN triple sum","Sigmoid neuron"],"version":1,"widths":{"m":[480,480,480,480,480,600,480],"math":[480,480,480,480,520,720,500],"visual":[720,760,720,720,720,780,720]}}
